A6L r5 review fix F37 (28 Sep 2026): in-call (downlink) volume of the q6voice VoiceMMode1 path.
VSS_IVOLUME_CMD_SET_STEP (0x000112C2, direction RX=1) on the full-control CVP session, as downstream msm voice.c
voice_send_vol_step_cmd() ("Voice Rx Gain"); ALSA control "VoiceMMode1 RX Volume Step" 0..15 (put returns the DSP
error and stores the step only when accepted), step kept per path and re-applied (non-fatal) at every path start.
Driven by a6l-q6voiced "volume <0..1>" from the audio HAL Telephony voiceVolume (audio/patches/0003).
Applies after a6l-q6voice-tx-mute-v75.patch (series kernel/rom-v2/series). Built W=1 against out-a6l-phone-v67.

